      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide**\n\n**Introduction**\nThe Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor is a compact, high-performance sensor designed for proximity detection applications. This guide provides a step-by-step introduction to getting started with the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor.\n\n**Hardware Overview**\nThe Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor features a 4-pin header (VCC, GND, SDA, SCL) and operates on a 5V DC input with a 3.3V logic output.\n\n**Setup and Initialization**\nTo initialize the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor, connect it to the I2C bus and assign the address via jumper. Run the initialization command '0x01' to wake the sensor.\n\n**Operating Characteristics**\nThe Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor operates within a temperature range of -40C to +85C and has a detection range of 2cm to 200cm.\n\n**Troubleshooting**\nIf you encounter any issues during setup or operation, refer to the troubleshooting guide below.\n\n**Troubleshooting Guide**\n\n*   Check the I2C bus connection and jumper settings.\n*   Verify the initialization command '0x01' is being executed correctly.\n*   Consult the datasheet",
      "source": "target",
